  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_12" name="Preparing-Owner Assignment and Allocation Validation" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Sources: docs/proposed-bpmn-catalog.md BPMN-12 and all catalog boundaries; Chapters/Kitchen406 - Capstone Paper.md SRS 4.15.2-4.15.3 FR-FUL-16-20,22-26; FR-STAFF-06; NFR-SEC-14, NFR-REL-03,05-06; BR-24,28-30,34. Website: index.html loads app/earnings-allocation.js (N.editor, N.read, allocation save, transition wrapper), app/fulfillment-state.js, app/subscription-batches.js and app/delivery-state.js. SRS governs differences: server-side validation and full previous/new allocation audit history are required even though the in-memory preview only partially implements these. Read top to bottom in internal responsibility lanes within one Kitchen406 pool; cross-lane links are sequence flows, not message flows. Authentication is an upstream precondition, Refer to BPMN-26 — User Authentication and Role-Based Access. Recheck authorization at protected actions here. Input: fulfillment ID, edit or validation-only mode, acting account, expected version, requested action and optional allocation draft. Output: saved or validated allocations with version, or rejected/cancelled outcome. Future call activities can invoke Process_16 in validation-only mode from BPMN-13/14/15/17; valid saved allocations require no human re-entry. No checkout, inventory reservation, production, courier booking, completion, cost calculation or reporting is executed here. A validation result does not authorize a later stale action: the fulfillment workflow must couple validation/version checks with their protected commit. Preserve original amounts and timestamps. Supporting batch control invokes this per fulfillment and reports independent results (FR-FUL-25), rather than applying one all-or-nothing batch. No other diagram is modified. All allocation validation steps and rejection outcomes are now visible on the main diagram. There are no embedded subprocesses or drill-down planes. Permission denial, stale version, invalid owner splits and incompatible locks each return a distinct reason. Rechecking controls at commit remains mandatory. Interactive edits may return to the editor or reload current fulfillment data for review.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_12">
