    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_16" name="Owner assignment or allocation check needed">
      <bpmn:documentation>One instance per fulfillment. Validation-only mode uses saved allocations. Edit mode may receive a proposed allocation/status draft from an operational screen. Historical completed records without allocations remain Unallocated (BR-30); do not invent ownership.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Load_16" name="Load fulfillment details and saved owner assignments">
      <bpmn:documentation>Read product-line identities and full quantities, eligible baking owners, saved percentages, operational role, expected/current version, status and courier lock state. Scope is one operational fulfillment, including one subscription week; the prepaid subscription purchase is not an allocation unit. Staff sees operational selections/percentages only, never allocated sales, costs, estimated profit or restricted analytics (FR-STAFF-06). On refresh, use the latest saved version and require fresh review and confirmation of any draft. Never replay a stale submission automatically.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_2</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_31</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Mode_16" name="Edit allocations?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Edit mode opens the reviewable draft. Validation-only mode reads and validates saved selections directly; it never prompts for owner choices or silently creates them. Unknown mode or missing context returns invalid through the shared validator.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_3</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:userTask id="Edit_16" name="Select owners and percentages for each line; review and confirm">
      <bpmn:documentation>FR-FUL-16-17,24. Display saved choices and whole line quantities. Select eligible Owner A at 100%, Owner B at 100%, or both. Newly selecting both proposes 50/50; allow Owner A an integer 1-99 and set B to 100 minus A. Apply-to-all affects only this fulfillment: retain and display existing per-line splits when applying both, using 50/50 only where no prior both-owner split exists. Review every affected line before confirmation. Selecting a single owner gives that owner 100%. The acting account is never assigned a share automatically. Locked records must not accept normal editing; a stale or forged draft is rejected by server validation. Cancel leaves all saved values unchanged.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_5</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_30</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Confirm_16" name="Confirmed?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_6</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_7</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="Cancel_16" name="Cancelled; saved state unchanged">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_6</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:businessRuleTask id="Permission_16" name="Check permission for the requested action">
      <bpmn:documentation>FR-STAFF-06; NFR-SEC-14. Check authenticated account operational permission for this fulfillment and action; validate request mode/context. Staff may record owners without viewing financial data or receiving an owner share. Authentication itself belongs to BPMN-26.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_7</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_8</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:businessRuleTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="PermissionValid_16" name="Permission granted?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_8</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_9</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_11</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="PermissionError_16" name="Explain permission denial">
      <bpmn:documentation>Report which permission is required for the requested action.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_9</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_10</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="PermissionRejected_16" name="Rejected: permission denied">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_10</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:businessRuleTask id="Version_16" name="Compare submitted and current order versions">
      <bpmn:documentation>FR-FUL-23; NFR-SEC-14. Detect a stale submitted version and flag the request for refresh.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_11</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_12</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:businessRuleTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="VersionValid_16" name="Order version current?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_12</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_13</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_15</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="VersionError_16" name="Explain what changed since review">
      <bpmn:documentation>Explain that the submitted version is stale and prompt for a refresh when applicable.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_13</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_14</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:businessRuleTask id="Allocation_16" name="Check eligible owners and percentages on every line">
      <bpmn:documentation>FR-FUL-16-18,24,26. Every product line requires exactly one valid allocation for the whole line quantity. Only the two eligible baking owners: A alone=100/0, B alone=0/100, both=integer A 1..99 and B=100-A. New both-owner selection defaults to 50/50; apply-to-all preserves and displays existing both-owner splits for review. Use draft for edits and saved values for validation-only. Staff action never implies a share. Historical completed items remain Unallocated, not retroactively inferred.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_15</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_16</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:businessRuleTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="AllocationValid_16" name="All line allocations valid?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_16</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_17</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_19</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="AllocationError_16" name="Explain missing/invalid assignments or percentages">
      <bpmn:documentation>Show the affected lines and what needs correction. A validation-only failure blocks the requested fulfillment action; an authorized edit must be requested separately.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_17</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_18</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:businessRuleTask id="Lock_16" name="Check completion and courier locks for this action">
      <bpmn:documentation>FR-FUL-19-20; NFR-SEC-14. Normal edits require incomplete fulfillment and no pending, booked, in-transit or unresolved courier booking. Failed/cancelled bookings may permit editing while incomplete. Validation-only checks lock compatibility with the requested action; do not reject valid saved allocations solely because normal editing is locked. Do not unlock records or grant a forbidden transition. The relevant fulfillment workflow handles payment, material and status checks.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_19</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_20</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:businessRuleTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="LockValid_16" name="Requested action allowed by locks?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_20</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_21</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_23</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="LockError_16" name="Explain completion or courier lock">
      <bpmn:documentation>Explain which completion or courier lock blocks the action. A later attempt must recheck the lock after it is resolved through its owning workflow.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_21</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_22</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="LockRejected_16" name="Rejected: requested action locked">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_22</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="SaveMode_16" name="Save confirmed edits?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Only a confirmed edit requests a save. Validation-only returns the existing valid saved allocation and checked version without changing history or fulfillment state.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_23</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_24</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_25</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="Validated_16" name="Saved assignments validated">
      <bpmn:documentation>Return allocation validation result and checked order version to BPMN-13/14/15/17. Those workflows handle preparation/ready, pickup completion, booking or cake handoff and all applicable non-allocation checks. Validation must remain coupled with the protected commit; no status transition is performed by this outcome.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_24</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Commit_16" name="Recheck permission, version and locks; save allocations and history atomically">
      <bpmn:documentation>FR-FUL-22-23,26; NFR-SEC-14 and NFR-REL-03,05. At commit recheck current authorization, eligible owners, order version and lock state; validation alone does not defeat a concurrent booking or completion. Save per-item previous/new owner selections and percentages, acting account and change timestamp with allocations and updated version. Avoid duplicate audit entries on repeated submission; unchanged values need no invented allocation change. Preserve stored product amounts, completion and allocation-lock timestamps. For a combined allocation/status request, participate in the fulfillment workflow’s single atomic transaction: commit neither unless every applicable transition/material check succeeds. Actual status/consumption/booking logic remains in BPMN-13/14/15/17; do not commit allocations separately ahead of a failed fulfillment transition. No owner financial amount or payout is calculated here.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_25</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_26</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Saved_16" name="Commit successful?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_26</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_27</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_28</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="Success_16" name="Allocations and change history saved">
      <bpmn:documentation>Return saved per-line allocations and new version. Subsequent changes follow the same permissions and lock rules. BPMN-39 uses preserved allocations for financial reporting separately. Allocation assignment does not establish fulfillment completion or a fulfilled sale.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_27</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Reject_16" name="Explain why allocations could not be saved">
      <bpmn:documentation>Report the exact failure, including permission, version, allocations, locks or save errors.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_28</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_29</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Recovery_16" name="How can this request recover?" default="Flow_16_32">
      <bpmn:documentation>Authorized interactive edits can correct invalid allocations when editing is allowed, or refresh and review after a stale version or retryable write error. For validation-only and combined requests, report the specific reason the fulfillment action is blocked. Permission denial, locks and non-retryable failures stop the request.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_14</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_18</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_29</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_30</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_31</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_32</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="ReturnError_16" name="Request blocked">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_32</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
